- content_for :title, "Privacy Policy - Typnix"

.max-w-4xl.mx-auto
  .bg-white.dark:bg-gray-800.rounded-lg.shadow-lg.p-8

    h1.text-3xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.dark:text-white.mb-6 Privacy Policy

    .text-sm.text-gray-600.dark:text-gray-400.mb-8
      | Last updated: December 18, 2025

    .prose.dark:prose-invert.max-w-none

      section.mb-8
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | Typnix (hereinafter referred to as "the Service") establishes this Privacy Policy (hereinafter referred to as "this Policy") regarding the handling of users' personal information as follows.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 1 (Personal Information)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | "Personal Information" refers to "personal information" as defined in the Personal Information Protection Act, which is information about a living individual that can identify a specific individual through the name, email address, or other descriptions contained in such information.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 2 (Methods of Collecting Personal Information)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4 The Service collects the following personal information when users register.
        ul.list-disc.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2.ml-4
          li Email address
          li Username
          li Google account unique ID (Google UID)
          li Profile image

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 3 (Purposes of Collecting and Using Personal Information)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4 The purposes for which the Service collects and uses personal information are as follows.
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li To provide and operate the Service
          li To respond to inquiries from Users
          li To inform Users about new features, updates, campaigns, etc. of the Service they are using
          li To contact Users as necessary, such as for maintenance and important notices
          li To identify Users who violate the Terms of Service or attempt to use the Service for fraudulent or improper purposes, and to refuse their use
          li To allow Users to view and modify their own registration information
          li To analyze and improve Service usage
          li For purposes incidental to the above purposes

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 4 (Changes to Purposes of Use)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li The Service may change the purposes of use of personal information only when it is reasonably deemed that the changed purposes are related to the original purposes.
          li When the purposes of use are changed, the changed purposes shall be posted on the Service.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 5 (Provision of Personal Information to Third Parties)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li The Service will not provide personal information to third parties without the prior consent of Users, except in the following cases.
          li.ml-6 When required by law
          li.ml-6 When it is necessary for the protection of human life, body, or property, and it is difficult to obtain the consent of the individual
          li.ml-6 When it is particularly necessary for improving public health or promoting the sound growth of children, and it is difficult to obtain the consent of the individual
          li.ml-6 When it is necessary to cooperate with a national agency, local government, or a person entrusted by them in performing legally prescribed affairs, and obtaining the consent of the individual may impede the performance of such affairs

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 6 (Disclosure of Personal Information)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li When requested by an individual to disclose their personal information, the Service will disclose it to the individual without delay. However, if disclosure falls under any of the following, the Service may not disclose all or part of it, and if a decision is made not to disclose, the Service will notify the individual of that decision without delay.
          li.ml-6 When there is a risk of harm to the life, body, property, or other rights and interests of the individual or a third party
          li.ml-6 When there is a risk of significant hindrance to the proper implementation of the Service's business
          li.ml-6 When it would violate laws and regulations

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 7 (Correction and Deletion of Personal Information)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li Users may request the Service to correct, add, or delete (hereinafter referred to as "Correction, etc.") their personal information held by the Service if the information is incorrect.
          li If the Service receives a request under the preceding paragraph and determines that it is necessary to respond to the request, it shall make the Correction, etc. of the personal information without delay.
          li When the Service makes Correction, etc. pursuant to the preceding paragraph, or makes a decision not to make Correction, etc., it shall notify the User without delay.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 8 (Suspension of Use of Personal Information)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li If requested by an individual to suspend or delete the use of personal information (hereinafter referred to as "Suspension of Use, etc.") on the grounds that the information is being handled beyond the scope of the purposes of use or that it was obtained by fraudulent means, the Service will conduct the necessary investigation without delay.
          li If, based on the results of the investigation in the preceding paragraph, it is determined that it is necessary to respond to the request, the Service will promptly suspend the use of the personal information.
          li When the Service suspends the use pursuant to the preceding paragraph, or makes a decision not to suspend the use, it shall notify the User without delay.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 9 (Use of Cookies and Other Technologies)

        h3.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-3.mt-4 9-1. Use of Cookies
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | The Service may use Cookies and similar technologies. These technologies help the Service understand the usage status of the Service and contribute to service improvement. Users who wish to disable Cookies can do so by adjusting their web browser settings. However, disabling Cookies may prevent the use of some features of the Service.

        h3.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-3.mt-6 9-2. Use of Google Analytics
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | The Service uses "Google Analytics," an access analysis tool provided by Google LLC (hereinafter referred to as "Google"), to understand the usage status of the Service and help improve it. Google Analytics uses Cookies to collect information about Users' use of the Service (access status, traffic, routing, etc.).
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | Data collected by Google Analytics is managed in accordance with Google's privacy policy. For Google Analytics Terms of Service and Google's Privacy Policy, please see the following URLs.
        ul.list-disc.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2.ml-4.mb-4
          li
            | Google Analytics Terms of Service:
            = " "
            a.text-blue-600.dark:text-blue-400.hover:underline href="https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/terms/jp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              | https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/terms/jp/
          li
            | Google Privacy Policy:
            = " "
            a.text-blue-600.dark:text-blue-400.hover:underline href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              | https://policies.google.com/privacy

        h3.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-3.mt-6 9-3. Use of Google AdSense (Planned)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | The Service may use "Google AdSense," an advertising service provided by Google, to support the operation of the Service in the future. Google AdSense uses Cookies to deliver advertisements based on users' interests.
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | Data collected by Google AdSense is managed in accordance with Google's privacy policy. For details, please refer to Google's Privacy Policy above.

        h3.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-3.mt-6 9-4. Opt-Out (Refusing Data Collection)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | Users can refuse data collection by Google Analytics and Google AdSense using the following methods.
        ul.list-disc.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2.ml-4
          li Disable Cookies from your browser's Cookie settings
          li
            | Install the Google Analytics Opt-out Add-on:
            = " "
            a.text-blue-600.dark:text-blue-400.hover:underline href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              | https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout
          li
            | Disable personalized ads from Google's ad settings page:
            = " "
            a.text-blue-600.dark:text-blue-400.hover:underline href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              | https://adssettings.google.com/

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 10 (Changes to Privacy Policy)
        ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.space-y-2
          li The content of this Policy may be changed without notice to Users, except for matters separately stipulated in laws and regulations or this Policy.
          li Unless otherwise specified by the Service, the revised Privacy Policy shall take effect from the time it is posted on the Service.

      section.mb-8
        h2.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-200.mb-4 Article 11 (Contact)
        p.text-gray-700.dark:text-gray-300.mb-4
          | For inquiries regarding this Policy, please use
          = " "
          a.text-blue-600.dark:text-blue-400.hover:underline href="https://forms.gle/a6EYBBxhMdGc4TJq6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            | this form
          | .

